Z||000000||n95265||03-12-99||02:27 PM||||I know this is open ended but...What should i be looking for when shopping for a Fiero...I am going to look at a 84 tonight.
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||03-12-99||02:54 PM||||Very good question. A lot of people buy a Fiero just on its looks alone and tend to forget it's a car that's at least 10 years old...<p>Here are a few tips:<p>- Before you enter the car, check for oil spots on the road under the car. This will tell you if the cars leaks oil or not.<br>- When you turn on the ignition, check to see if the "Check Engine Soon" light comes on (it's on the dashboard). If it doesn't, the bulb has been removed to hide a problem with the car. Ask why the bulb has been removed.<br>- Check the headlights. A lot of Fieros have broken headlight motors. Check to see if they open and close properly.<br>- Start the engine and immediately check the idle RPM. It is quite normal if idle varies between 800-1000. The ECM is trying to find the proper idle RMP. If it varies more than that, there might be a problem.<br>- Find a place (preferably a large parking space) where you can test the brakes. Drive the car at around 15mph and slam the brakes. Do not release the brakes after you have come to a full stop. The brake pedal should be steady. If it is slowly moving down, there's a problem with the brakes.<br>- On an open space, come to a full stop. Turn the steering wheel all the way to one side and slowly make a full turn. Do the same thing with the steering wheel turned the other way. If there's a problem with the steering, you should feel that right away.<br>- As soon as temperature hits 160F, check idle again. It should be steady.<br>- After the testdrive, check the engine compartment. If there are signs of fresh oil, or smoke is coming from the compartment, it has an oil leak somewhere.<br>- Check the handbrake. Most of the time it is broken...<p>These are some checks you can do. There are many more things you could check but this is from the top of my head (somebody slammed into my Fiero today, so I'm a bit pre-occupied now!).<br>
Z||000002||n95265||03-12-99||07:50 PM||||Thanks for the info...I bought it...$700 it runs fine...think i need new shocks/struts..kinda shimmys down the road...other than that thing runs great.
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||03-12-99||10:49 PM||||I wish I could find a decent car for $700.. ;)<p><br>That sucks.. how bad was the damage to your Fiero?
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||03-13-99||12:29 AM||||Well, it's kind of a long story and the damage is mostly to the paint...<p>I was backing up out of a parking space (after checking there was no traffic nearby ofcourse) very slowly. When I was halfway out, I really couldn't see if any traffic was coming anymore because of the dead spot, but I was going so slowly that if any car would be coming, he could easily go around me or stop in time. Then suddenly this guy with his VW Rabbit slammed his car into the back of mine. He never tried to avoid me, or try to stop or honk his horn for that matter. His car was a very old one, so I guess he was just after the insurance money. He got out of his car and immediately started yelling (without even checking for any damage) that it was all my fault and that I must be drunk to pull out like that. So I told him that he could have easily stopped and that he never tried to avoid the collision. Only after 5 minutes or so did he check his car for damage and told me how lucky I was that he didn't have any damage and he got in his car and drove away. I did got his license plate number so I will go to the police today.
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||03-14-99||04:37 PM||||n95265:<p>700 bucks? Heck if I new that, my tip would have been "ask him for the keys"!<p>:)
Z||000006||n95265||03-16-99||06:48 PM||||yep...$700  New tires..1 right front upper ball joint and that was it...passed inspection today...the only problem is with the way it looks, the paint is BAD i can see the black under the paint it has faided so bad.  So far i think it is the best 700 i have spent.
Z||000007||raceknb||03-18-99||07:33 PM||||You might want to take you car down to an Auto Salon and have them detail it.  I was under the impression that the body panels on the fiero wern't painted, but rather dyed.  Had my 86 buffed out and looks great.  It was black, but had faded to almost a white color and now...*SHINE*  Good luck and hope you enjoy yours as much as I do mine. ( I just love stepping on the gas a flying past little Miata's and 300zx's(older ones of course))
Z||000008||theogre||03-31-99||07:16 PM||||I got that one beat $650us. Why? when comming home one night previous owner snaged mirror with mini van on slick driveway.<p>Other than that I've replaced some of the usual wereouts. 115K.... things like the TPS are just too old to fool with, and with the amount I drive,,, I don't trust stuff like that to not fail in the worst place it could. And the water pump let go... no big suprise. I don't think I have 1500 total in it yet.
Z||000009||862M4inCA||12-20-1999||05:17 AM||||Since were on the subject of purchase prices. I've got that $650 beat with my $500 US. Didn't think it was a bad buy. Only thing I've really had to do was change the cat so it would pass smog. Glad I bought it since I totaled my other car a couple months after I bought my Fiero.<p>[This message has been edited by 862M4inCA (edited 12-20-1999).]||||reg||6
Z||000010||Scott2M4||12-20-1999||08:17 AM||||Gosh, Cliff.  I'm really sorry to hear about this!  Hope you're OK, though ... physically, I mean.<P>Man, what is it with Fiero crashes lately!?  First, the Fiero split in half by a full-size truck, then the newspaper picture showing the remains of a totaled notchback, now word of fieroshop's trashed SE and Cliff's damaged GT!<P>OK - this is to whomever (or whatever) is out to get our Fieros!  My 87SC is still original and it's gonna stay that way!!!  Got it!!!???  Same goes for many others on this forum!!!  Go find some VW Corrados or something!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||4
