Z||000012||Monkeyman||12-20-1999||01:24 PM||||Cliff--Can your car be fixed?  Do we need to send you some parts?  Or is it totalled (God forbid!)?  I can send you some chicken soup.  My grandmother always gave some to me when I was sad (tho I don't know why--must be a grandma thing!).  Did you cuss the guy as he drove off?  I'd have said things that he would have to look up in the dictionary.  It's not like you have a black car or anything.  I don't understand why.....Oh, nevermind.  I'm getting pi**ed and it's not even my car.  Hi.  My name is Dave and I'm a Fieroholic.||||reg||1
Z||000013||PAUL88GT||12-20-1999||01:26 PM||||I got my first Fiero (86 2M4) about two years ago at an auction for $325. I drove it home (about 50 miles).  Since then I have replaced the tires, the alternator, and some interior parts. It has faded red paint and torn seats, but runs good.  This one got me hooked and I later bought an 88gt after reading the forum.||||reg||7
Z||000014||mshill||12-20-1999||04:54 PM||||I just got my 86GT home on Saturday.  Bought it for $500.  The exterior is pretty shot. Someone (way back when) painted dark blue metal flake over a nice black car moulding, dew wipes and all.<P>Except for a MAJOR oil leak (rear valve cover) and a gerry-rigged clutch slave (broken mount bracket) the car is in great mechanical condition.  It has the lowered performance springs with new KYBs all around and 50 series tires on 15 inch rims.  The sucker is so low that I had a hard time getting it onto the U-Haul.<P>It is unfortunate the guy didn't have more mechanical know-how or the exterior would be in much better shape.  It ended up sitting outside for the last 3-4 years. Then again, I wouldn't have gotten it for so cheap.||||reg||10
Z||000015||kong||12-20-1999||09:22 PM||||I .got my 87 notchback for $700. 4cyl,5spd,new paint and new tires. I got it cheap because it needed a clutch,and the guy didn't want to work on it. He said it was too much of a pain in the @$$. I had the new clutch in in 1 day, and been driving it everyday for 2 yrs now with no problems (except for a water pump)People are amazed that I have kept it. I'm 6'4 and they can't believe that I can get in and out of it. Well I'll rambled on long enough cya later.||||reg||10
Z||000016||geyser||12-21-1999||12:24 AM||||My first Fiero was free. I rescued it from a fire department extrication class, 86 SE v6 with all the options. I just bought an 87 GT, very happy. Kong, I'm 6'5" 220lbs and fit just fine.||||reg||1
